Z||000000||Philphine||06-04-2001||12:13 PM||||i've bit off way more than i can chew. guess i'll be hitting the local library, but i'm wondering if some chevy smallblock v8 reading can be reccommended. i'd like to get as good a laymans understanding as i can. specifically pre-'86 ('67-'70?) an opportunity may be coming my way and i'll need it. also, is there a way of checking a bare block for cracks and/or wear beyond machining? i've gotten a nice size block fairly cheap (302/327? the seller wasn't sure,said he got it at an auction himself, but it has this casting #3892657 and building date code e 14 7) but i'll need to know if it's worth basing an engine on. thanks for any help. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (project. or at least an interesting collection of parts)<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-04-2001||12:48 PM||||You could have the block Magnflux and/or Zyglo treated. Zyglo will find surface cracking fast. Magnaflux will find cracks below surface. Neither is cheap.<P>A dealler part desk may be nice and tell you what the casting is for certain, but even then you'll have to have the block fully dimensioned to see what if any machine work has been done to it and what it still need if anything. <P>Your first issue is... Unless you can verify the block has it's original main caps in the original positions the block will probably have to be align bored to make sure the main bearings will be right. This is a very critical job. The block is essentially junk unless this is 100% right.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||06-04-2001||12:56 PM||||I got a lot of good info for classic cars/engines off another Pontiac site (www.classicalpontiac.com) just flip threw their forums for a while, the have some really good info.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||06-04-2001||12:56 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.mortec.com/castnum.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mortec.com/castnum.htm</A> <P>CASTING#.....SIZE...YEAR...MAIN CAP BOLTS....NOTES<BR>3892657....302.....67....2...Z-28 Camaro<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Paul<BR>||||reg||1
